## ══ Session — rate-limit deadline fix & multi-brand reorganization ══

### 21. [2026-03-12] --till should not count rate-limit wait time
--till (hh:mm or n hrs) sometimes encounters rate limit approaching. and when we wait for the reset, this waiting time should not be counted in of the operation time. for ex. if we wait extra 3 hrs for resetting token limit, we should run 3 more hours to sum up the original n hrs.

### 22. [2026-03-12] Multi-brand output reorganization (claude/gemini/codex)
I am going to expand the model to different brand (gemini, codex) and their different models (gemini3 pro, flash, gemini 2.5 pro, flash), and codex (5.4, 5.3 codex, 5.2 codex, 5.2), so our output/* must be re-organized to output/gemini output/codex output/claude, right? and the models will be more than just claude (4.6 opus, 4.6 sonnet). note that output/* changed to 3 brands, then our showoff_4review must follow that.

### 23. [2026-03-12] FHL MCP Server research
fhl (bible.fhl.net) they claims to have mcp capabilities, check for that, see if we can get the qb.php qp.php,etc, api json data from mcp instead.

Result: Found ytssamuel/FHL-MCP-Server — a local Python wrapper, not a remote service. Same bible.fhl.net API behind the scenes. 27 tools. Not integrating now. Report saved to FHL_MCP.md.

### 24. [2026-03-13] Rename llm_direct_sn_unv2lcc → llm_direct_sn_unv2notyet + multi-version support
refactor llm_direct_sn_unv2lcc into llm_direct_sn_unv2notyet, introduce a --target-version lcc (default) or other 版本縮寫 (rcuv2010, tcv, esv, nasb...). output/ folder should be moved one level above to output/{version}/{brand}/{Book}/{Chap}/{verse}.json. --set-target-version for other version's coworkers. Version-specific JSON fields (lcc_sn, rcuv2010_sn), per-version system prompts (system_prompt_lcc.md), showoff viewer version selector with localStorage memory.

### 25. [2026-03-13] --chineses accepts multiple books
--chineses 利 民 and --chineses 利, 民 and --chineses 利,民 and --chineses 利 should all work. nargs='+' with comma-split normalization.

### 26. [2026-03-13] Preserve token percentage for colleagues + verse time report
I want you to always preserve 30% token for my colleagues, enter pause/wait for next reset whenever we are 70% rate limit/token used. Introduced --preserve-token-percentage-4-colleagues (default 30) with cost-based budget learning from .window_budget.json. Also moved 📊 progress summary after Saved line, added ⏱ verse time report.

### 27. [2026-03-13] Linux compatibility — update all usage instructions to python3
I want to expand the project to also work on linux. Tested llm_direct_sn_unv2notyet by running 申命記 chap 1 for 10 verses — all passed. The code is already cross-platform; the only fix was updating all usage instructions from `python` to `python3` across docstrings and CLAUDE.md files.

### 28. [2026-03-13] Hot-reloadable .run_config.conf — on-the-fly parameter changes
Replace .target_version single-value file with .run_config.conf (bash-style NAME=value). Hot-reloaded every ~10s during runs. File always wins over CLI args. Parameters: TARGET_VERSION, TILL, VERSE_COUNT, PRESERVE_TOKEN_PERCENTAGE, PAUSED. Set PAUSED=true to pause at next verse, false to resume. CLI args merge into config at startup. Migration from old .target_version on first run.

### 29. [2026-03-13] Aggressive defaults + config template cleanup
Aggressive refactor: remove --no-work-hours-stop and --immediately-restrict-first-session flags. Default to NO preserve-token limit (was 30%) and NO work-hours pause (was ON). Config keys now match CLI arg names (lowercase with hyphens: target-version, till, verse-count, preserve-token-percentage-4-colleagues, work-hours-start, midnight-resume-at, quit-at-work-hours, paused). CLI args override config for session only — NOT persisted to file. Template config has only target-version and paused active, rest commented out with examples. Long sleeps (rate-limit, preserve-token, work-hours) now use interruptible 30s chunks with config hot-reload.

### 30. [2026-03-13] Remove .target_version migration + snapshot-delta priority model
Remove stale .target_version migration code that kept re-creating config with rcuv2010. Implement snapshot-delta priority model: CLI args win at startup, config file state is snapshotted (snapshot1). During hot-reload, only keys that changed from snapshot1 are applied — overriding even CLI args. Unchanged keys keep their startup-resolved value. This cleanly resolves the design conflict between CLI and config file priority.

### 31. [2026-03-13] Add max/min verse time to progress summary
Add per-verse time tracking (max/min) to the 📊 progress line. Shows after 2+ verses: `📊 3 verses done, 3min working, 0.9 min/verse, max 90s, min 30s`.

### 32. [2026-03-14] Add Ollama local LLM as new "local" brand
sai.fhl.net has NVIDIA GB10 GPU + 119GB RAM with Ollama already running in Docker on port 11434. Added `call_ollama()` using Ollama REST API (`/api/generate`) with `_extract_json()` fallback for unreliable JSON output. New brand "local" in MODEL_BRAND_MAP. Models: qwen3:32b, qwen3:30b, qwen2.5:72b/32b/7b, llama3.3:70b, llama3.1:70b/8b, gpt-oss:120b (already pulled by colleagues on sai.fhl.net). Brand-based dispatch in process_sec(): local→call_ollama(), else→call_claude(). Skip preserve-token logic for local (no shared budget). Added --ollama-url (default http://localhost:11434).

### 33. [2026-03-14] --model --help detailed model/brand reference
Added `--model --help` (or `--model -h`) that prints a detailed table of all models grouped by brand, with notes, recommendations (★ qwen3:32b for Chinese), and usage examples. Main `--help` now says "Use --model --help for full list" instead of listing all models inline.

### 34. [2026-03-14] Implement Gemini and Codex (OpenAI) brands via CLI tools
I want to implement the full chatgpt/gemini brands/models too. I want to save money, so we will use existing gemini/codex auth (login) instead of api key. For codex (openai) models, they are gpt-5.4, gpt-5.3-codex, gpt-5.2-codex, gpt-5.2; for gemini cli modes, they are gemini-2.5-pro, gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-3-pro-preview, gemini-3-flash-preview. Added `call_gemini()` using `gemini -p -y --output-format stream-json` with `parse_gemini_stream_json()`. Added `call_codex()` using `codex exec --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox --json --output-schema` with `parse_codex_jsonl()` (handles item.completed, turn.completed, turn.failed, error events; schema requires `additionalProperties: false` for OpenAI). Brand-based dispatch dict in process_sec(). Preserve-token logic now Claude-only. Tested: gpt-5.2 Gen 1:1 → 0.96 confidence; gemini-2.5-flash Gen 1:1 → 0.95 confidence; gemini-3-flash-preview Gen 1:1 → 1.0 confidence (perfect SN match).

### 35. [2026-03-14] Show brand/model during LLM invocation
between the LCC: and LCC+SN: output lines, add a line showing which brand/model is being invoked: `⚙ Invoking {brand}/{model} for SN embedding...` so the user knows which LLM is working.

### 36. [2026-03-14] Fix CLI check + progress tuple unpacking for non-claude brands
Startup always required `claude` CLI even for local models — fixed to only check the CLI matching the brand. Also fixed `call_ollama()` unpacking `progress` as 2 values when it's a 3-tuple `(total_processed, start_time, total_paused)`.

### 37. [2026-03-14] OSS model benchmark on sai.fhl.net
Benchmarked local models on sai.fhl.net (NVIDIA GB10, 119GB RAM) for Gen 1:1–3. qwen3:32b is the only usable local model (confidence 0.9–0.98, ~8–15 min/verse). qwen3:30b and gpt-oss:120b both failed to produce structured JSON (confidence 0.3). Cloud models (gemini-3-flash-preview 1.0, codex/gpt-5.2 0.96, claude/sonnet ref) remain superior. Results documented in OSS_MODEL.md.

### 38. [2026-03-14] Document confidence scoring basis & update CLAUDE.md
把這些關鍵評分與 LLM 自評分的根據或者參考細節寫在 CONFIDENCE_BASIS.md. Created CONFIDENCE_BASIS.md documenting the two-layer quality assessment: (1) LLM self-reported confidence (subjective 0.0–1.0 with tier table), (2) verify_sn_coverage() objective SN count check. Documents special values (0.3 = JSON parse fallback, 0.0 = error), model-specific observations, and reprocessing threshold (0.85). Updated CLAUDE.md with llm_direct_sn_unv2notyet component section linking to both CONFIDENCE_BASIS.md and OSS_MODEL.md. Also cleaned up system_prompt_lcc.md (removed duplicate/garbage content after line 41).

### 39. [2026-03-14] Add gpt-5.1-codex-max and gpt-5.1-codex-mini models
add models: gpt-5.1-codex-max and gpt-5.1-codex-mini. Added to MODEL_BRAND_MAP as codex brand and --model --help notes.

### 40. [2026-03-14] Add qwen3:8b local model
Colleagues added qwen3:8b on sai.fhl.net. Added to MODEL_BRAND_MAP as local brand and --model --help notes.

### 41. [2026-03-14] Fix codex JSON parse failures via --output-last-message
Read side efforts (strong_number_embedding_gemini, strong_number_embedding_codex) to compare. Found codex fork uses `codex exec --output-last-message <file>` which writes clean final answer to a file — no thinking text contamination. Adopted this for call_codex(): replaced `--json` + `parse_codex_jsonl()` with `--output-last-message` + `_extract_json()`. Also switched from `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` to `--sandbox read-only`. Tested: Gen 1:1 went from 0.3 (parse fail) to 0.72, Gen 1:4 went from 0.3 (parse fail, +6 extra SNs) to 0.95 with perfect SN coverage.

### 42. [2026-03-15] Add Google TranslateGemma support (all 12 variants)
go to sai and run code there. Add Google's TranslateGemma support — translation-specific model (55 languages incl. Chinese) built on Gemma 3. Added all 12 variants to MODEL_BRAND_MAP: 3 base (4b/12b/27b) + 9 instruction-tuned (4b/12b/27b × q4_K_M/q8_0/bf16). Pulled all models on sai.fhl.net via `docker exec ollama ollama pull`. Ollama on sai runs in Docker container, not bare metal.

### 43b. [2026-03-15] Dynamic model version in output path
rename sonnet into sonnet-4.6 and opus to opus-4.6, make sure internally it is identified correctly. How do guarantee that when output, as time flies, you will record correct version number on the fly? no hard coded. Solution: resolve claude model alias at startup via one quick CLI call — `claude --model sonnet --output-format stream-json` returns `system.model: "claude-sonnet-4-6"`. Cached for the session. Output path and JSON now record the actual resolved model ID (e.g. `output/lcc/claude-sonnet-4-6/`). Non-claude brands (gemini, codex, local) are already version-specific — no change needed.

### 43a. [2026-03-15] Flexible --sec argument
let --sec support multiple verses like 1 2 3 4 or 1,2,3,4, or 1, 2, 3 ,4 ,5 or 1,2, 5-13,17,19. Added parse_sec_arg() supporting space-separated, comma-separated, ranges, and mixed formats. --sec now accepts nargs="+" with flexible parsing.

### 43. [2026-03-15] Refactor output/ path: brand → model segment
do you think we should expand our spec, that the output/ area is like output/version/model/book/chap/? add a model segment in between, the same name as --model? Changed output path from `output/{version}/{brand}/` to `output/{version}/{model}/` with sanitized names (colon→underscore). Fixes collision where all local Ollama models shared `output/lcc/local/`. Updated save_result(), skip-check, generate_manifest.py, generate_data_bundle.py, start_server.py (/api/target-sn now uses model= param). Created migrate_output_brand_to_model.py for one-time data migration. `--brand` flag kept as internal dispatch mechanism (picks which CLI to call).

## ══ Session 03533f85 — survey1 founding: 3-model gold standard ══

### 44. [2026-03-18 ~08:00] survey1 inception
I want you to do a llm_direct_sn_unv2notyet/survey1/ sub program, to work out a better version of the prompt sent to LLM. show me your current prompt of doing sn embedding

### 44a. [2026-03-18 ~08:10] Multi-agent team approach
I want to use your agent team capabilities, calling gemini and codex, to work out a better result, go /plan to discuss

### 44b. [2026-03-18 ~08:20] Stage 1 clarification — gold standard, not optimization
note that, we are not at stage2, improving our prompt or algorithm, for other cheap/free models to optimize. we are at stage1, to establish the 'best' result

### 44c. [2026-03-18 ~08:30] Prompt evolution during gold standard production
wait, but you may be right, that our original prompt might need to evolve during the stage 1 golden result production. why not? but how does it (the original prompt) evolve, once it improves, do we need to re-test?

### 44d. [2026-03-18 ~08:40] Round 1 strict unanimous, Round 2-3 majority
第一輪嚴格一點, 一旦沒有三者一致, 不是多數 2/3 決, 而是直接進入第二輪, 第二輪輪流當裁判觀看先前紀錄, 第二輪起才是 2/3 多數決

### 44e. [2026-03-18 ~08:50] 回測 sampling rules
一旦 prompt 有改, 雖然這一節取得通過, 但是必須回頭驗證過往已經同意的歷史經節, 特別是以往超過第一輪進入第二輪甚至第三輪的, 一定要回測新的prompt. 曾經造成 prompt 修改過的必定要測, 進入第二輪的要挑出 50% 來測, 進入第三輪的 80%, 第一輪全同意的要挑出 20% 來回測. 回測可以照第一二三輪規則通過. 一旦沒有通過, 則這個規則改動必須重來.

### 44f. [2026-03-19 ~00:10] v1.1 draft plan
先根據 1:1-1:3 的 judge 修正，草擬 v1.1 prompt → 回測 → 刪除 v1.0 結果 → 從頭跑

